# arena_loadstore.tkr — the §16 arena-mmap sub-crumb B fixture. `main.tks` maps one anonymous
# private page via `teko::sys::syscall6(sys::SYS_MMAP, ...)`, guards the returned address is
# positive (a valid mapping — never casts a negative errno-band `i64` to `u64`), stores a
# sentinel 64-bit word at that address via `teko::mem::store_u64`, reads it back via
# `teko::mem::load_u64`, unmaps the page via `teko::sys::syscall2(sys::SYS_MUNMAP, ...)`, and
# exits 0 only if the loaded word matches the stored sentinel and the unmap succeeded. The
# harness observes exit code 0, proving the C-leg `load_u64`/`store_u64` emitters
# (`emit_load_u64`/`emit_store_u64`, `src/codegen/codegen.tks`) round-trip a real word through
# real mmap'd memory.

Feature: arena_loadstore — the §16 C-leg load_u64/store_u64 emitters round-trip a word through mmap'd memory

  Scenario: store_then_load_u64_roundtrips_through_mmap_and_exits_zero — the process maps a page, stores a sentinel word, loads it back, unmaps, and exits 0
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 0
